{
  "name": "CRYPTO 01 — Price Alert Multi-Token (Telegram)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 10
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "sched",
      "name": "Check Every 10 Minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        240,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "w1",
              "name": "watchlist",
              "value": "=[\n  { \"name\": \"KINS/SOL\", \"chain\": \"solana\", \"pair\": \"F42tZnKPavq1VUcrL6ymhc6YqVpt84fWwgzbNTv2wb3W\" },\n  { \"name\": \"WBNB/USDT\", \"chain\": \"bsc\", \"pair\": \"REPLACE_WALLET_CONTOH\" },\n  { \"name\": \"CAKE/WBNB\", \"chain\": \"bsc\", \"pair\": \"REPLACE_WALLET_CONTOH\" }\n]",
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "id": "w2",
              "name": "threshold_persen",
              "value": "5",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "watchlist",
      "name": "Token Watchlist",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        460,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Expand the watchlist into one item per token\nconst wl = $json.watchlist;\nconst out = [];\nfor (const t of wl) {\n  out.push({ json: { name: t.name, chain: t.chain, pair: t.pair, threshold: $json.threshold_persen } });\n}\nreturn out;"
      },
      "id": "split",
      "name": "Split Per Token",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        680,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "=https://api.dexscreener.com/latest/dex/pairs/{{ $json.chain }}/{{ $json.pair }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
      "id": "fetch",
      "name": "Fetch Price (DexScreener)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        900,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse price and check the threshold\nconst pair = $json.pair || $json.pairs?.[0];\nif (!pair) return [{ json: { error: 'pair not found' } }];\n\nconst name = $('Split Per Token').item.json.name;\nconst threshold = $('Split Per Token').item.json.threshold;\n\nconst price = parseFloat(pair.priceUsd || 0);\nconst chg = parseFloat(pair.priceChange?.h24 || 0);\nconst liq = parseFloat(pair.liquidity?.usd || 0);\nconst vol = parseFloat(pair.volume?.h24 || 0);\nconst mcap = parseFloat(pair.marketCap || pair.fdv || 0);\n\nconst rp = n => '$' + Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });\nconst triggered = Math.abs(chg) >= threshold;\n\nlet message = '';\nif (triggered) {\n  const direction = chg > 0 ? '🚀 UP' : '🔻 DOWN';\n  message = direction + ' *' + name + '*\\n\\n';\n  message += 'Price: ' + rp(price) + '\\n';\n  message += '24h change: *' + chg.toFixed(2) + '%*\\n';\n  message += '24h volume: ' + rp(vol) + '\\n';\n  message += 'Liquidity: ' + rp(liq) + '\\n';\n  if (mcap > 0) message += 'Market Cap: ' + rp(mcap) + '\\n';\n  message += '\\nTime: ' + new Date().toISOString();\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    name, price, change_24h: chg, liquidity: liq, volume_24h: vol,\n    market_cap: mcap, triggered, message\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "parse",
      "name": "Check Threshold",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1120,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.split }}",
              "rightValue": "true",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "if-alert",
      "name": "Move > Threshold?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1340,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "sendMessage",
        "chatId": "REPLACE_CHAT_ID",
        "text": "={{ $json.message }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "parse_mode": "Markdown"
        }
      },
      "id": "send",
      "name": "Send Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1560,
        220
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Telegram Bot"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CRYPTO 01 — Multi-Token Price Alert\n\n**Flow:**\nEvery 10 minutes → check the price of every token in the watchlist → if the move exceeds the threshold → send a Telegram alert\n\n**What to edit:**\n- `watchlist` in the *Watchlist Token* node — add or change tokens\n- `threshold_persen` — default 5%\n- `GANTI_CHAT_ID` — your Telegram chat ID\n\n**How to get a pair address:**\n1. Open dexscreener.com\n2. Search for your token\n3. Copy the pair address from the URL\n\n**No API key needed** — DexScreener is free.\n\n**Example watchlist entry:**\n{ \"nama\": \"KINS/SOL\", \"chain\": \"solana\", \"pair\": \"F42tZn...wb3W\" }",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "note",
      "name": "Panduan",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        160,
        100
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
